<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Kenneth Mitchell</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/</link><description>Recent content on Kenneth Mitchell</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Thinking Hard or Hardly Thinking?</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/thinking-hard-or-hardly-thinking/</link><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/thinking-hard-or-hardly-thinking/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This post is very much inspired by and in direct response to Ben Kuhn&amp;rsquo;s short post &lt;a href="https://www.benkuhn.net/thinkrealhard"&gt;think real hard&lt;/a&gt;. Kuhn introduces and briefly interrogates a hilariously reductive problem-solving technique commonly attributed to Richard Feynman:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write down the problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think real hard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write down the solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When I read this, it makes me think of this image:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/thinking-hard-owl.png" alt="A two-panel drawing tutorial that jumps from two ovals to a finished owl" width="530" height="453" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At first glance, this advice is not terribly useful, and likely the last thing that people want to hear when working on hard problems: &amp;ldquo;Have you tried thinking about it yet?&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>SF Coast</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/sf-coast/</link><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/sf-coast/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Isla Mujeres</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/isla-mujeres/</link><pubDate>Sat, 25 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/isla-mujeres/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Fleet Week</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/fleet-week/</link><pubDate>Sat, 11 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/fleet-week/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Cats</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/cats/</link><pubDate>Sat, 27 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/cats/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Monaco</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/monaco/</link><pubDate>Sun, 06 Jul 2025 11:38:36 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/monaco/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Èze</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/eze/</link><pubDate>Sun, 06 Jul 2025 09:24:11 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/eze/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Marseille</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/marseille/</link><pubDate>Thu, 03 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/marseille/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Port Vendres</title><link>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/port-vendres/</link><pubDate>Tue, 01 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.kenneth-mitchell.com/photos/port-vendres/</